The rotation discussion has isolated one fermionic minus sign. A second, closely related sign appears when identical particles are exchanged. For a two-particle wavefunction, $\begin{aligned}
P_{12}\Psi_B(1,2)&=+\Psi_B(1,2)=+\Psi_B(2,1),\\
P_{12}\Psi_F(1,2)&=-\Psi_F(1,2)=-\Psi_F(2,1).\end{aligned}$ Bosonic states are symmetric and fermionic states antisymmetric.

